# r136fresh_1108 (11-08): FRESH t=0 R136a1 deep B = Caltech r136a1_128_B.athinput (md5 3d48ea84a1412084706dddc72188dff1) + keys marked '# mkdeck (r136fresh_1108)'
# (made by /raven/ptmp/jinma/r136fresh_1108/jobs/mkdeck.py; key lists jobs/keys_current.txt [+ jobs/keys_variant.txt for *_variant]; see ../DECKS.md).
# SPONGE keys (problem/he_sponge_rate, _r0, _mode, _dmax) = Caltech's; expected to be replaced by a ramped sponge (r136seam_1108 diagnosis).
<comment>
r136a1-1104 PHASE 1 DEEP B (USER 11-04 late: inner boundary log T 6.5, lean grid to 100 Rsun, 128^2; REPLACES the 512 first look).
  Star: Keszthelyi+2025 MESA (zenodo 15702085, CC-BY-4.0) TS = MLT++ (compact), v_init 200 km/s, M_init 281.8 Msun, midMS:
  M 233.9 Msun, log L 6.833, R_ph 24.91 Rsun, Teff 59.1 kK (tables/EOS X 0.58, Y 0.4136, Z 0.0064).
  x1min 19.45 Rsun (log T 6.50, radiative in MESA: nabla_rad/nabla_ad 0.972 MESA kappa / 0.986 ours; 0.30 Msun above; below
  the MLT++ envelope CZ base 20.6 Rsun); column F_MLT := 0 below 20.6 Rsun and the wall flux = L/(4 pi x1min^2) (pure radiative).
  x1max 100 Rsun (USER variant B, lean). sp WEDGE theta pi/3..2pi/3, phi 0..pi/3 (periodic), 128 x 128; radial grid leanB831 (831 cells: dr 0.06 Rsun
  base, 0.011-0.012 Rsun on 24.2-25.9 = 7+ cells/H_p at the compact Fe peak, 0.04 Rsun on 27-40 Rsun (where the run is),
  0.15 at 50, 0.6 at 65, 1.5 at 100). IC tools/ic_star mode mesa; inner boundary wall + WB + n2 seed (as RSG E / HG / BSG).
  OPACITY = MIXED SOURCE (USER 11-04): Rosseland = MESA r24.08.1 kap a09 X 0.58 Z 0.0064 (log R in [-8,1]), TOPS of the same
  composition outside; Planck = LANL TOPS X 0.58 Z 0.0064 AGSS09; tables on log T 3.50-7.00 (T7).
  NO LINE FORCE (CAK) in phase 1: any wind Mdot / v_inf from this run is NOT PHYSICAL.
  See /resnick/groups/carnegie_poc/jingze/r136a1_1104/SETUP.md (section 8).
